# Git Commits

- Commit **only when the user asks**.
- Use [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/):

```
<type>(optional-scope): <short imperative summary>
```

Types: `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `style`, `docs`, `test`, `chore`, `perf`, `ci`.

Examples:

- `feat(auth): add login page and auth store`
- `fix(users): correct empty-state when list is empty`
- `chore: set up folder structure and eslint`
- `refactor(ui): extract Button into components/ui`

## Rules

- One logical change per commit when possible.
- Message explains **why**, summary stays under ~72 chars.
- Never commit secrets (`.env`, credentials).
- Never use `--no-verify` unless the user explicitly requests it.
- Never amend/push unless the user asks.

If the user asks for a vague dump commit ("save everything"), suggest splitting into meaningful Conventional Commits and explain briefly.
